A B-tree organizes keys so an equality lookup navigates a balanced tree. Traversal is logarithmic in indexed entries, but total query cost also includes matches, visibility checks and possible heap access. A small table may still be cheaper to scan. This complete fixture inserts the row before selecting it.

Run this declared setup in a fresh database before the query below:
```sql
CREATE TABLE customers(id int PRIMARY KEY,email text,signup_date date);
INSERT INTO customers VALUES(1,'user@example.com','2026-09-24');
CREATE INDEX idx_customers_email ON customers(email);
```

An index on (customer_id,order_date) sorts primarily by customer and then date. Equality on the leading key plus a date range directly matches that ordering. Filtering only on a later key is not universally forbidden: the planner may scan the index or use version-dependent strategies, whose cost depends on data. Inspect the actual plan.

Run this declared setup in a fresh database before the query below:
```sql
CREATE TABLE orders(id int PRIMARY KEY,customer_id int,order_date date,total_amount numeric(10,2));
INSERT INTO orders VALUES(5,101,'2026-02-01',120);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_cust_date ON orders(customer_id,order_date);
```

Indexes consume storage and add maintenance work. Do not equate an insert with a fixed count of physical writes. PostgreSQL uses MVCC and WAL; eligible HOT updates can avoid new index entries, and index cleanup for deleted versions is coordinated with vacuum. In pg_stat_user_indexes, relname is the table name and indexrelname is the index name. Sizes depend on data and environment; no fixed byte count is promised.

Run this declared setup in a fresh database before the query below:
```sql
CREATE TABLE orders(id int PRIMARY KEY,customer_id int,order_date date,total_amount numeric(10,2));
INSERT INTO orders VALUES(5,101,'2026-02-01',120);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_cust_date ON orders(customer_id,order_date);
```

EXPLAIN shows an estimated plan. EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) executes the query and reports measured behavior. Never run a mutating EXPLAIN ANALYZE on valuable data without an appropriate disposable transaction. An Index Only Scan still may fetch heap pages for visibility checks unless the relevant pages are marked all-visible. Plans and timings depend on version, statistics, visibility and data, so the example below has no universal exact plan.

Run this declared setup in a fresh database before the query below:
```sql
